  "id": "COMPOUND:30682 - PROTEIN:4911",
  "verbalization": "Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside appears to be a target of multiple compounds, including SNU-387, S-ethylcysteine zwitterion, and Dendocarbin K, all of which are implicated in targeting the CD276 antigen. This suggests a potential mechanism where Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside may act as a modulator or activator of these compounds, which in turn interact with CD276. The evidence indicates that the compound may influence the expression or activity of CD276 through a series of molecular interactions, possibly involving downstream signaling pathways. The consistent presence of CD276 as a target across different compounds supports the idea that Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside could be a key player in the regulation of CD276, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the compound's potential role in modulating CD276 expression, potentially through a complex network of interactions that are yet to be fully characterized.",
